WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.770 --> 00:00:06.020
I bet there's 100 answers
to this question.

00:00:06.020 --> 00:00:09.232
But in the end,
the thing that matters most to me and

00:00:09.232 --> 00:00:12.294
if you think about it,
I bet matters most to you,

00:00:12.294 --> 00:00:16.540
which is your family and
your extended network of friends.

00:00:16.540 --> 00:00:20.090
In the end, that is super important.

00:00:20.090 --> 00:00:24.377
So while we get wrapped around the axle
of doing whatever we're doing,

00:00:24.377 --> 00:00:28.460
it is really important to remember
that that's what matters most.

00:00:29.530 --> 00:00:31.910
I'll say the other thing is perspective.

00:00:31.910 --> 00:00:36.136
And this has been one of the delights of
being married to a neurosurgeon okay,

00:00:36.136 --> 00:00:38.390
what we do in business is important.

00:00:38.390 --> 00:00:39.490
It's incredibly important.

00:00:39.490 --> 00:00:44.680
It's important to the employees of HP to
our bars, but no one gets hurt at HP.

00:00:44.680 --> 00:00:45.180
No one dies.

00:00:46.290 --> 00:00:50.294
And so remembering what's really
important is I think critical,

00:00:50.294 --> 00:00:55.220
and I'll tell you a little story which
I've told on a number of occasions.

00:00:55.220 --> 00:00:59.826
So one of my closest friends from Harvard
Business School, who was in my section,

00:00:59.826 --> 00:01:01.782
had a great career in Los Angeles.

00:01:01.782 --> 00:01:05.452
And has two children who are about
the same age as my children, and

00:01:05.452 --> 00:01:10.210
her 24-year old went into the Green Berets
and was killed in Afghanistan in June.

00:01:11.320 --> 00:01:13.263
So when things seem pretty tough,

00:01:13.263 --> 00:01:16.950
remember your 24-year old did
not get killed in Afghanistan.

00:01:18.030 --> 00:01:21.970
So I think you've just got to
remember what actually matters here.

00:01:21.970 --> 00:01:23.970
And it's great to be wrapped up in work.

00:01:23.970 --> 00:01:28.392
It's terrific but in the end that is
the perspective of what is really,

00:01:28.392 --> 00:01:31.240
really important here honestly.

00:01:31.240 --> 00:01:35.068
And I will say when I lost the governor's
race, it was hard to have that perspective

00:01:35.068 --> 00:01:37.390
because it's what it could have,
should have.

00:01:37.390 --> 00:01:41.390
If I'd done this, if I'd done that maybe
it would have turned out differently.

00:01:41.390 --> 00:01:44.250
In the end, nothing really bad happened.

00:01:44.250 --> 00:01:46.150
I lost the governor's race.

00:01:46.150 --> 00:01:51.310
And my family was intact, my husband was-,
you just have to remember.

00:01:51.310 --> 00:01:55.320
And then last but not least,
I would say, your reputation.

00:01:55.320 --> 00:02:00.140
You have to be known as high integrity,
doing what you say saying what you mean

00:02:00.140 --> 00:02:05.055
because everything can go away and
if you still have your integrity, intact.

00:02:05.055 --> 00:02:10.629
And so often at eBay at HP I often ask
what is the right thing to do here?

00:02:10.629 --> 00:02:14.457
And it's challenging because the right
thing to do is quite different in

00:02:14.457 --> 00:02:16.110
different cultures.

00:02:16.110 --> 00:02:20.577
And I always used to say to our teams, it
may be different in different countries.

00:02:20.577 --> 00:02:24.412
But if your mother or your father or
someone you love your children were

00:02:24.412 --> 00:02:29.800
reading the New York Times, and they knew
what you were doing, would they be proud?

00:02:29.800 --> 00:02:33.099
Or if they were sitting in the eve of
the conference from watching the decision

00:02:33.099 --> 00:02:35.760
making process would they be proud of you?

00:02:35.760 --> 00:02:39.523
And that's the ultimate question
whether you're from Asia or

00:02:39.523 --> 00:02:41.726
from Latin America, or for Europe.

00:02:41.726 --> 00:02:46.299
Usually having that notion of what would
your parents think transverses all those

00:02:46.299 --> 00:02:49.627
cultural norms about what's acceptable and
what's not.

00:02:49.627 --> 00:02:54.481
So, I think those are the three
things that I'd point to right away.

